// What searching the ground turns up, by table (old FeatureFactory forage tables). A terrain or cave
// names its table in terrain.json; a named place carries its own in locations.json. Finds per hour
// are density x abundance; each find weighs between minKg and maxKg. Loaded once by Content.
// Rates are what a person really gathers (#152): a first hour on fresh good ground gives about 300 g of
// fibre, 200 g of birch bark and 30 g of resin on forest, 100 g of willow bark on marsh and 50 g of flint
// on rock. Each resource rose by one factor in every row of it, here and in locations.json, so a place
// keeps its edge over plain ground (flint_seam's flint and Birch Stand's bark set apart); stone, shale,
// branches and food are as they were. Report.HaulText measures a first hour and a day of it.
